  "quotes": [
    { "text": "In lesson one, we set the stage. In lesson two, we start performing.", "approx_timestamp": "0:17" },
    { "text": "Just like with AI coding, Agentic Coding is easy to start, hard to master. All the low hanging fruit is getting chewed up. It's time to do the smart work, not the hard work, to get asymmetric return on your engineering.", "approx_timestamp": "0:44" },
    { "text": "If you pay attention, you can see the aspects that never change and you can place big bets on them.", "approx_timestamp": "1:14" },
    { "text": "Plan, code, test, review, document.", "approx_timestamp": "1:52" },
    { "text": "We're not here to write bigger prompts and iterate back and forth and back and forth. We're here to dial up the autonomy knob all the way to 11.", "approx_timestamp": "2:05" },
    { "text": "Adopt your agent's perspective.", "approx_timestamp": "2:56" },
    { "text": "Your agent is brilliant, but blind.", "approx_timestamp": "3:04" },
    { "text": "Agents are ephemeral, no context, no memories, and no awareness outside of what you give it. And when all the work is done, it resets back to zero.", "approx_timestamp": "3:12" },
    { "text": "Your agent needs your context, your model, your prompt, and your tools — the core four.", "approx_timestamp": "3:35" },
    { "text": "It's not about what you can do anymore. It's about what you can teach your agents to do.", "approx_timestamp": "4:08" },
    { "text": "We want the longest hot streak possible of success. When you stack up these leverage points, Agentic Coding success becomes inevitable.", "approx_timestamp": "4:57" },
    { "text": "Your agent can only see what you let it see.", "approx_timestamp": "11:05" },
    { "text": "Not only do we have bad code, we have bad agentic code.", "approx_timestamp": "12:03" },
    { "text": "I'm not actually fixing the issue. I'm setting up my codebase so that my agent can resolve the issue.", "approx_timestamp": "13:32" },
    { "text": "Types tell a story about how information travels throughout your codebase.", "approx_timestamp": "18:28" },
    { "text": "Types are IDKs — information dense keywords. They point to exact locations in your code base and represent the flow of a specific type of information.", "approx_timestamp": "20:32" },
    { "text": "If it's hard for you, you should assume it'll be hard for your agent.", "approx_timestamp": "22:01" },
    { "text": "Consistency is a powerful actor against complexity for both humans and for agents.", "approx_timestamp": "22:24" },
    { "text": "It's so important and widespread that I've called this the agent navigation problem.", "approx_timestamp": "22:33" },
    { "text": "Your agent will make mistakes, okay, just like you... The only question is, does it have the right leverage it needs to correct the mistakes?", "approx_timestamp": "27:52" },
    { "text": "If you're not writing tests, you're probably vibe coding.", "approx_timestamp": "29:11" },
    { "text": "Put simply, plans are just prompts. Put accurately, plans are how you communicate massive amounts of work to your agent.", "approx_timestamp": "30:14" },
    { "text": "The plan is the prompt, and that means great planning is great prompting.", "approx_timestamp": "31:21" },
    { "text": "ADWs are created when you combine one or more agentic prompts right out of the commands directory and then you wrap it in arbitrary code and then you kick it off autonomously with a trigger.", "approx_timestamp": "32:14" },
    { "text": "If you don't measure it, you can't improve it.", "approx_timestamp": "34:42" },
    { "text": "We're not aiming to become a babysitter for AI agents. We're looking for one shot solutions.", "approx_timestamp": "36:31" },
    { "text": "Once you start one-shotting, don't break the streak.", "approx_timestamp": "37:57" },
    { "text": "This is not the end game. This is the early game.", "approx_timestamp": "38:42" },
    { "text": "Are you still manually looking at error messages? Stop. Stop.", "approx_timestamp": "40:57" },
    { "text": "Three time makes a pattern. Three time should trigger your engineering brain. Automate.", "approx_timestamp": "42:31" },
    { "text": "It's not about you anymore. It's about what you can do for your agent so they can work for you.", "approx_timestamp": "43:15" },
    { "text": "English is the new programming language.", "approx_timestamp": "45:31" },
    { "text": "Master the primitives and you'll master the compositions.", "approx_timestamp": "46:08" }
  ],
